.TH DANBY-CHAOSMAP 1
.SH NAME
danby-chaosmap \- logistic-map bifurcations, cobwebs, and Lyapunov exponent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/chaosmap
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Chaosmap
iterates the difference equation
.EX
x[n+1] = r x[n] (1-x[n]).
.EE
The left view is a bifurcation diagram: after transients are discarded, it
plots long-run values against the parameter.  The orange line marks the
selected parameter.  The right view is a cobweb construction between the map
and the diagonal, exposing each iteration geometrically.
.PP
The heading reports a finite-sample Lyapunov exponent.  A negative value means
nearby states contract in the sampled orbit; a positive value means exponential
separation and is evidence of chaos.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the bottom track to choose
.IR r .
Drag in the cobweb view to choose the initial value.
.B R
restores the reference case, and Escape or
.B Q
exits.
.SH VALIDATION
Regression tests check the fixed point at
.I r=2,
a negative exponent in the period-two regime, and the known exponent
.I log(2)
at
.IR r=4 .
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/danby/chaosmap.m
.br
.B /appl/danby/chaosmap.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/chaosmap.b
.SH SEE ALSO
